"Act as a Senior Systems Architect and conduct a comprehensive, component-by-component diagnostic of your current OpenClaw configuration and execution environment. My system is currently experiencing significant latency and running very slowly.

Please review your entire configuration file, internal architecture, and recent execution behavior to identify bottlenecks, errors, or inefficiencies. Specifically, analyze and report on the following areas:



API & Model Routing: Evaluate all configured LLM endpoints (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter, or local models). Are there timeout configurations that are too generous? Are we experiencing rate-limiting, or using heavy/expensive models for simple routing tasks that could be handled by faster, smaller models?



Context & Memory Management: Analyze how short-term and long-term memory (vector databases) are handled. Is context bloat occurring? Are we passing unnecessarily large token payloads in every loop? Check the chunking and retrieval configuration.



Agent Execution Loop & Tool Calling: Inspect your core reasoning loop. Are there blocking synchronous operations that should be asynchronous? Look for redundant tool calls, excessive retries, or recursive loops.



System & Environment: Check for any poorly optimized local scripts, memory leaks, or inefficient file I/O operations within your working directory.

Output a detailed diagnostic report categorizing your findings into:



Critical Errors: Things broken or failing.



Performance Bottlenecks: Things slowing the system down.



Suggested Optimizations: Best-practice improvements for speed and efficiency.

For every issue found, provide the specific, actionable code snippet or configuration change required to fix it."